#: _speech_core/settings/number_processing_panel.py:223
msgid "NVDA native is the safe default and leaves numbers unchanged for NVDA and the active synthesizer. Threshold digit spelling only rewrites standalone integer strings at the selected length or longer. Phone number processing handles common U.S.-style phone numbers as grouped digits when enabled. Friendly toll-free prefixes say numbers like 1-800 as one eight hundred. Currency processing can say simple dollar amounts as dollars and cents for synths that do not. Ordinal processing can say standalone tokens such as 1st and 22nd as words. ISO year-first recognition handles strict four-digit year-first dates such as 2026-09-05 without changing the selected numeric date format. When Windows locale is enabled, unsupported Windows date formats fall back to the selected numeric date format. Currency, times, non-phone codes, and alphanumeric strings are left unchanged."
msgstr ""

